On Sun, Apr 20, 2008 at 1:24 PM, Vid Sintef <picos.picos@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> I wonder what kind of meaning a CAhA can bear by governing a sumti. In
> {ka'e mi do viska}, for example, what would be the translation of the
> sumti tcita (ka'e mi)?

I don't think {ka'e mi} makes much sense. I think the sumti tagged by {ka'e}
gives the conditions for the possibility, so I would expect {ka'e lo nu ...}.
For example

  do viska lo ragve be le bitmu ka'e lo nu do me la superman
  "You could see behind the wall if you were Superman."

mu'o mi'e xorxes


